    "notes": [
      {
        "category": "summary",
        "text": "Security update for libarchive",
        "title": "Title of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "description",
        "text": "This update for libarchive fixes the following issues:\n\n- creating temporary files in the current working directory instead of the target directory can lead to file creation\n  failures when the working directory is not writable (bsc#1254340).\n- file descriptor leak in the mtree parser cleanup path could lead to file descriptor exhaustion and denial of service\n  (bsc#1261003).\n- NULL pointer dereference in archive_acl_from_text_w() could lead to a segmentation fault (bsc#1260998).\n- reading from an invalid index when buffer size is smaller than H_LEVEL_OFFSET can lead to an out-of-bounds buffer\n  overrun (bsc#1254341).\n- incorrect pointer handling for RAR5 files declaring over 8192 filters can lead to excessive resource usage and denial\n  of service (bsc#1261002)\n",
        "title": "Description of the patch"
      },
      {
        "category": "details",
        "text": "SUSE-SLE-Micro-6.0-840",
        "title": "Patchnames"
      },
